{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214148-2e-how-to-fight-the-walker-in-darkness","id":1214148,"title":"[2E] How to Fight the Walker in Darkness?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-05-02T07:20:38-07:00","id":1214148,"title":"[2E] How to Fight the Walker in Darkness?","content":"Thanks in advance for thoughts and suggestions.<br /> <br /> I have a party of Essence 5, soon-to-be Essence 6 Solars, a full Circle, who have set themselves in opposition to the Walker in Darkness. They have discovered a way to render his immortality non-functional, and they plan to attack him shortly thereafter.<br /> <br /> To begin, I have changed the canonical Deathlord powers to remove all Solar Charms (so he has all Abyssal Charms for which he meets the prereqs), removed Solar-Circle Sorcery (so he has merely all three Circles of Necromancy and the first two Circles of Sorcery), and gave him the mote pool of a ghost.<br /> <br /> This still makes him nigh invincible.<br /> <br /> Even before his perfect defenses, his scene-long Melee Charms make him practically unassailable. The PCs simply don't have enough dice to reduce his DVs to a manageable level. <br /> <br /> Short of crippling him even further, what suggestions do you all have for how to beat someone with a static Melee PDV in the range of 23?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T07:39:36-07:00","id":1214152,"title":"","content":"Get him alone, prevent him from fleeing and then the slow process of mote draining. <br /> <br /> Had the same fight but against First and Forsaken as the end of my first long 2E fight think it went a few hundred ticks and really boiled down to getting the deathlord to spend more then motes then he recovered but also the fight was set up in such a way that there was a slight chance they would eventually negate his perfect defense through flaw of invulnerbility and they eventually did so which settled things.<br /> <br /> About the PDV it really depends on the player characters more then potential ways to beat it which is pretty easy if you build a circle of E6 solars for the purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3085-chance","name":"chance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T07:55:35-07:00","id":1214159,"title":"","content":"Weaken him<br /> <br /> The Deathlords get their power from the Neverborn - sneak into the underworld and mess with the Neverborn that powers the Walker. Sure, it wont be easy, but compare it to taking the one ring and tossing it into the fires of mount doom: It will rob the walker of his powers.<br /> <br /> As a ghost he'll have a fetter or two - control over those would grant you control over the ghost, assuming that you know the right bits of sorcery or necromancy. Seek those fetters, steal them, and then use that attack or mess with him.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or maybe strike up the ruling gods of Great Forks. They spun a prophetic story about the potential future defeat of another deathlord. Maybe see if you can get them to do something similar for the walker? It might not be easy.... it might require one of those fetters, so they can have something to bind the prophecy to?<br /> <br /> It's your classic &quot;You have to go on a quest to find the thingy that'll reveal/exploit/be the weakness of the big bad&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T08:20:49-07:00","id":1214170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214148-2e-how-to-fight-the-walker-in-darkness#post1214148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short of crippling him even further, what suggestions do you all have for how to beat someone with a static Melee PDV in the range of 23?</div> </div> </div> </div>This really depends on how the PC's are a built, but in general they're in serious trouble. There are a lot of issues with the 2nd edition paradigm, especially once Solar-tier characters get to Essence 7+ levels where static dice pools + extremely long-duration Charms + artifacts can easily make an elder Exalt effectively untouchable even to heavily min-maxed player characters.<br /> <br /> First, your players can rely on attacks that bypass Parry so they only have to go for his Dodge DV (but that's probably still fairly high) or attacks that bypass both Parry and Dodge, but those tend to be fairly expensive and probably not all of your PCs have access to them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise with a static DV of 23, your players will generally need to be rolling around 40 dice to have chance of hitting, but their dice pool (after spending Essence) is only 23 (including specialties). Somehow they're going to need to scrape up another 17 dice on average just to have a chance to hit him. Unless you provide your players with some kind of plothax boost that lets them bypass their own dice caps, or artifacts that give an insane number of bonus dice to hit, there's not going to be much they can do.<br /> <br /> So nerfing him a bit further is probably the easiest way. You can do this behind-the-scenes by lowering his dice caps - say Deathlords don't have actual Solar/Abyssal tier Charms, but Arcanoia that can do a lot of similar things but don't have the same dice cap. Maybe he can only add Essence to his dice pool instead of Attribute + Ability, and maybe the duration is only a turn instead of for an entire Scene.<br /> <br /> Alternatively if you want the players to be able to defeat Walker in Darkness but still want Deathlords to otherwise remain untouchable and use Abyssal Charms, you could have the players do something on-screen to weaken him - perhaps they get a unique type of poison (maybe provided by a rival like the Mask of Winters), or figure out a way to curse him (webkilla's idea pf the Great Fork gods is a good one) in order to weaken him to the point where they can engage with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-02-2018, 11:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T10:31:50-07:00","id":1214212,"title":"","content":"Going strictly by MoEP: Abyssals. Do everything you possibly can to make him gain Resonance because an eruption at essence 10 is supposed to be way worse than anything in the book (with the Lion being sealed in his armour given as an example) so get him there and potentially sit back and watch as the Neverborn drag him away kicking and screaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12844-bladewind","name":"Bladewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-02T17:56:44-07:00","id":1214375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214148-2e-how-to-fight-the-walker-in-darkness?p=1214170#post1214170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This really depends on how the PC's are a built, but in general they're in serious trouble. There are a lot of issues with the 2nd edition paradigm, especially once Solar-tier characters get to Essence 7+ levels where static dice pools + extremely long-duration Charms + artifacts can easily make an elder Exalt effectively untouchable even to heavily min-maxed player characters.<br /> <br /> First, your players can rely on attacks that bypass Parry so they only have to go for his Dodge DV (but that's probably still fairly high) or attacks that bypass both Parry and Dodge, but those tend to be fairly expensive and probably not all of your PCs have access to them.<br /> <br /> Otherwise with a static DV of 23, your players will generally need to be rolling around 40 dice to have chance of hitting, but their dice pool (after spending Essence) is only 23 (including specialties). Somehow they're going to need to scrape up another 17 dice on average just to have a chance to hit him. Unless you provide your players with some kind of plothax boost that lets them bypass their own dice caps, or artifacts that give an insane number of bonus dice to hit, there's not going to be much they can do.<br /> <br /> So nerfing him a bit further is probably the easiest way. You can do this behind-the-scenes by lowering his dice caps - say Deathlords don't have actual Solar/Abyssal tier Charms, but Arcanoia that can do a lot of similar things but don't have the same dice cap. Maybe he can only add Essence to his dice pool instead of Attribute + Ability, and maybe the duration is only a turn instead of for an entire Scene.<br /> <br /> Alternatively if you want the players to be able to defeat Walker in Darkness but still want Deathlords to otherwise remain untouchable and use Abyssal Charms, you could have the players do something on-screen to weaken him - perhaps they get a unique type of poison (maybe provided by a rival like the Mask of Winters), or figure out a way to curse him (webkilla's idea pf the Great Fork gods is a good one) in order to weaken him to the point where they can engage with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>While it would result in a vulnerability to countermagic, an essence 6 character could produce a weapon with a total of +14 accuracy, +20l/2 damage, +12 defense, and a rate of 14, which deals Agg. to ghosts, were you willing to slaughter a lot of ghosts before your fight, by using the Blind Edge spell.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, that vulnerability to countermagic renders it essentially worthless as is, since it's necromancy vs a master necromancer. Well, unless you use a magical flurry to blitz him down the moment you make contact with him, before he can deploy countermagic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/357-plotvitalnpc","name":"PlotVitalNPC","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T07:16:00-07:00","id":1214589,"title":"","content":"These are all good suggestions! I think I'm going to have to let the ritual that removes his immortality weaken the Deathlord as well. Otherwise, he's just too powerful. <br /> <br /> Thank you all, and if anyone has more suggestions, I'd love to hear them!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T07:48:09-07:00","id":1214599,"title":"","content":"The RAW way to beat a Deathlord in 2.0 (including right out of the box via Flaws to Essence 5) requires two characters<br /> <br /> - one is the area defender who runs an infinitely-looped unsurprise-able perfect defense, while redirecting all attacks to him. A standard way to do it is a Solar perfect, Joy in Adversity for mote regen, and a scene-long surprise negator (preferably Eyes of the Unconquered Sun).<br /> <br /> - one is a Solar Circle Sorcerer who casts Rune of Singular Hate on the Deathlord. Per RAW, RoSH doesn't have keywords. It can only be counterspelled (but Deathlords can't cast Solar Circle), sundered by a couple of charms (but those are attacks so get redirected and perfected by Character #1), corded (avoidable by right timing), or suppressed by a couple of vanishingly rare effects (and if those are active you'll be having other problems anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T08:06:19-07:00","id":1214607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octopoid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214148-2e-how-to-fight-the-walker-in-darkness#post1214148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short of crippling him even further, what suggestions do you all have for how to beat someone with a static Melee PDV in the range of 23?</div> </div> </div> </div>With Essence 6 Charms (whether accessed naturally or at E5 via charms) Solars beat 23 DV. At a minimum your players need Honored Companion of the Sun and Panoptic Fusion. There are many other straight dice-adders (I won't be making a list now but I've done so in the past); and all these are before the Solars actually running a real optimized attack. <br /> <br /> An optimized attack can be done in many, many ways. Common ones for Solars include running the needed regeneration/discounts to constantly spam doubling successes, unblockable/undodgeable tags, hit with 0 or 1 success minumum tag, add high Virtue rolls, redirecting successes via Crane, or Bloodied King builds. If Brutal Attack isn't banned, some of these get even higher.<br /> <br /> A fully-built E6 Solar can expect to hit the equivalent of ~100 accuracy at least on some of his attacks, and without using any TO exploits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T09:27:54-07:00","id":1214642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>emeraldstreak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214148-2e-how-to-fight-the-walker-in-darkness?p=1214599#post1214599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- one is a Solar Circle Sorcerer who casts Rune of Singular Hate on the Deathlord. Per RAW, RoSH doesn't have keywords. It can only be counterspelled (but Deathlords can't cast Solar Circle), sundered by a couple of charms (but those are attacks so get redirected and perfected by Character #1), corded (avoidable by right timing), or suppressed by a couple of vanishingly rare effects (and if those are active you'll be having other problems anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is how my PCs beat him in the game's finale.<br /> Two of them and an NPC used Rune of Singular Hate on him, and this lowered his Essence to 0, at which point his soul dissolved. (It could have required more or less Runes, depending on rolls. Tbh, after two, or probably even 1, I think they could have beat him in a fight, but he'd already killed the Full Moon in one attack so they were panicking.)<br /> <br /> Of course, casting Rune of Singular Hate does screw you up, but it was the game's finale (after, what, 4 years or something?). And when we later restarted the game in 3rd ed, it was a good reason to let me start the game at Essence 4 instead of Essence 5, as they'd lost their Essence 5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T19:04:38-07:00","id":1214876,"title":"","content":"I banned perfect defences in my 2nd ed game because the combat paradigm they create does not resemble &quot;fun&quot; to me. I do have some experience with that type of combat though. <br /> <br /> <b>The Mote Attrition Game</b>:<br /> Fight him in Creation so you have easier time regaining motes than he does. This one is obvious, but may require set-up to draw him out. <br /> <br /> You need cheap ways to force him to spend motes. He has scene long defences. If the PCs are throwing less dice than his DV, he doesn't need to spend motes to be relatively safe. That's bad. Those scene-long defences do not negate penalties from co-ordinated attacks, only normal onslaught. Use co-ordinated attacks to tank his DV and force him to spend motes on either a perfect or an Instant penalty-negator like Dipping Swallow, without spending as many motes of your own. <br /> <br /> Use unblockable attacks if he relies on Parry, undodgeable if he relies on Dodge. Yes, his perfects negate the unblockable or undodgeable quality, but if he doesn't use those Charms he has to rely on his inferior DV, so doing this forces him to spend those motes. Remember that he can only have one Infinite Ability Mastery active at once. <br /> <br /> Use things like cover and environmental penalties to force him to spend more motes to hit you. <br /> <br /> <b>Outlasting Death</b><br /> Bring in an Earth Dragon stylist to break his shit. He'll be somewhat less scary without his panoply of horrors. <br /> <br /> If he doesn't rely on Parry or Dodge but rather on Resistance perfects, that means you're more likely to get hits in, they just won't do damage. Use this to apply non-damage effects that require a successful strike. <br /> <br /> A useful ally NPC might be a dedicated healer. <br /> <br /> There are no attacks of opportunity in this system. Run away if you need to, hide behind the allied army you brought with you, and regroup. You did bring an army, right?<br /> <br /> <b>Killing the Bastard</b><br /> Once he's vulnerable and can't perfect, have your Martial Arts specialist grapple him, and then everyone else hits him with everything they have while his DV is inapplicable. It's brutally effective, just ask the 3rd circle demon my players demolished that way. <br /> <br /> <b>As the ST</b><br /> Give him a Flaw of Invulnerability that is actually exploitable and give the PCs an opportunity to discover it and engineer the situation so they can exploit it. <br /> <br /> In Exalted, players know dice pools before they declare their defences, but you don't have to play the Walker as if he has this perfect knowledge. Have him occasionally not commit as much as he should to his defence against a PC who seems less of a threat. Have him activate defensive Charms when he doesn't really need to. <br /> <br /> Come up with a reason he wouldn't just flee once the PCs have run him out of motes. <br /> <br /> Consider introducing other secrets that your players can discover and exploit. He doesn't remember his life before becoming the Walker in Darkness, but as far as we (the fans) know, he was a Zenith caste (probably) follower of Kal Bax who died in the Invisible Fortress some time after the Usurpation, slain by the Twilight who would become the Mask of Winters. Give the PCs a chance to figure out who he once was, and use that against him. Maybe a reminder of who he was that causes him to hesitate. Maybe an Eclipse oath that still binds him that they can trick him into breaking so that he is cursed to botch spectacularly. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Measure of Hope is right about everything.&quot; - Wise Old Guru<br /> <br /> Currently running an Exalted 2.5 Abyssals game in a homebrew modern shard because I value neither my time or my sanity, and I'm loving almost every minute of it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23907-measure-of-hope","name":"Measure of Hope","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"190"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-03T21:23:25-07:00","id":1214905,"title":"","content":"Wasn\u2019t there a line of thought to summon a Hidden Judge of the Sacred Flame, who cannot be hurt by the Walker in Darkness, to tank while you made with the mojo in the background?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-04T08:01:33-07:00","id":1215057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Measure of Hope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1214148-2e-how-to-fight-the-walker-in-darkness?p=1214876#post1214876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe an Eclipse oath that still binds him that they can trick him into breaking so that he is cursed to botch spectacularly.</div> </div> </div> </div>OOOOOOOOOH, I like!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>DrLoveMonkey - &quot;On the other hand having a warhammer that's basically a steel beer keg on the end of a seven foot pole is fucking awesome.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9453-octopoid","name":"Octopoid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9453_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"424"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}